## feat(kg-ui): modal popup for empty Filter-tab search results

**Context:** In the Graph Explorer Filter tab, a search that matched nothing only updated a small inline info line ("No entities found matching the filter criteria."), which was easy to miss. The message is now surfaced via a centered modal popup.

**Changes:**
1. `src/front/static/global/js/utils.js` — Added reusable `showInfoDialog({ title, message, okText, okClass, icon })` helper (single OK button, auto-cleanup on dismiss) and exported it on `window`.
2. `src/front/static/query/js/query-sigmagraph.js` — In `_executeGraphSearch`, the empty-seeds branch now also calls `showInfoDialog({ title: 'No results', icon: 'search' })` (guarded by a `typeof` check) while still updating the inline info text as a fallback.

**Modified files:**
- `src/front/static/global/js/utils.js`
- `src/front/static/query/js/query-sigmagraph.js`

**Test result:** No automated tests cover this JS UI. Lint clean on both files; full suite unchanged (see below).

